{"path":"string/byte/strcat","title":"std::strcat","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>strcat","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/byte/strcat","section":"string","kind":"page","summary":"Appends a copy of the character string pointed to by src to the end of the character string pointed to by dest. The character src[0] replaces the null terminator at the end of dest.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/cstring\">&lt;cstring&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> strcat<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> dest, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> src <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Appends a copy of the character string pointed to by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">src</span></code> to the end of the character string pointed to by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">dest</span></code>. The character <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">src<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span></span></code> replaces the null terminator at the end of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">dest</span></code>. The resulting byte string is null-terminated.\n</p><p>The behavior is undefined if the destination array is not large enough for the contents of both <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">src</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">dest</span></code> and the terminating null character.\n</p><p>The behavior is undefined if the strings overlap.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> dest\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> pointer to the null-terminated byte string to append to\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> src\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> pointer to the null-terminated byte string to copy from\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">dest</span></code>\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Because <code>strcat</code> needs to seek to the end of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">dest</span></code> on each call, it is inefficient to concatenate many strings into one using <code>strcat</code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cstdio&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cstring&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> \n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> str<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"nu0\">50</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Hello \"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> str2<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"nu0\">50</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"World!\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">strcat</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>str, str2<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">strcat</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>str, <span class=\"st0\">\" Goodbye World!\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/puts\"><span class=\"kw1846\">std::<span class=\"me2\">puts</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>str<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Hello World! Goodbye World!</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/byte/strncat\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>strncat</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  concatenates a certain amount of characters of two strings <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/byte/strcpy\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>strcpy</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  copies one string to another <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/string/byte/strcat\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>strcat</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"string","title":"Strings library"},{"path":"string/byte","title":"Null-terminated byte strings"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::strcat","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Appends a copy of the character string pointed to by src to the end of the character string pointed to by dest."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"dest, src"},{"label":"Return value","note":"dest"},{"label":"Notes","note":"Because strcat needs to seek to the end of dest on each call, it is inefficient to concatenate many strings into one using strcat."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"strncat","note":"concatenates a certain amount of characters of two strings"},{"label":"strcpy","note":"copies one string to another"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":190,"codeBlockCount":2}
